/*
  AnimatedNumber.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0075 · AnimatedNumber (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web source
  (components/data-display/AnimatedNumber.tsx) renders NO translatable copy: it displays only a
  formatted number bracketed by a caller-supplied `prefix` / `suffix` (themselves caller data, not
  this component's copy, exactly as in the web props). There are therefore no message keys to mirror —
  this catalog is intentionally free of copy keys, and the Swift sources hold no English literals.

  The surface's only locale-sensitive output is the number itself: grouping separators and the decimal
  mark. That localization is bound through the injected `Locale` (AnimatedNumberInput.locale →
  AnimatedNumberFormatting.string), the native parity of the web `fmtNumber` global-locale read, rather
  than through a string table. The per-surface table name ("AnimatedNumber") is reserved here so the
  file-set stays consistent with its sibling surfaces and folds into the app `Localizable.xcstrings`
  master catalog at integration time should localizable chrome ever be added.
*/
